Let's break down this Terraform data source step-by-step like a DevOps engineer would understand in real AWS environments.

Your code:

data "aws_vpc" "prod_vpc" {
  filter {
    name   = "tag:Name"
    values = ["production-vpc"]
  }
}
This Terraform block searches AWS and fetches an existing VPC whose tag Name = production-vpc.

It does NOT create anything. It only queries AWS and returns information.

1. What data Means in Terraform
data "aws_vpc" "prod_vpc"
Structure:

data "<PROVIDER>_<RESOURCE>" "<LOCAL_NAME>"
Explanation:

Part	Meaning
data	Terraform keyword for reading existing infrastructure
aws_vpc	AWS data source type
prod_vpc	Local name used inside Terraform
So Terraform internally stores this as:

data.aws_vpc.prod_vpc
You can access attributes like:

data.aws_vpc.prod_vpc.id
data.aws_vpc.prod_vpc.cidr_block
2. What AWS API Terraform Calls
When Terraform runs:

terraform plan
Terraform internally calls AWS API similar to:

DescribeVpcs
Then it filters VPCs using your filter condition.

Flow:

Terraform
   │
   │ AWS Provider
   │
   ▼
AWS API → DescribeVpcs
   │
   ▼
Return matching VPC
3. Understanding the filter Block
Your code:

filter {
  name   = "tag:Name"
  values = ["production-vpc"]
}
This block tells Terraform how to search the VPC.

Structure:

filter {
  name   = "FILTER_FIELD"
  values = ["VALUE"]
}
4. name = "tag:Name"
This means:

Search using AWS tag called "Name"
AWS resources often have tags like:

Key: Name
Value: production-vpc
Example VPC in AWS:

VPC ID	Tag Name
vpc-123abc	production-vpc
vpc-456def	dev-vpc
Terraform filter:

tag:Name = production-vpc
So Terraform finds:

vpc-123abc
5. values = ["production-vpc"]
This means acceptable values for that filter.

Terraform supports multiple values.

Example:

values = ["production-vpc","prod-network"]
Terraform will search:

tag:Name = production-vpc OR prod-network
6. Why values is a List
Even if you give one value, Terraform requires a list.

So syntax must be:

["value"]
Not:

"value"
Example valid:

values = ["production-vpc"]
Example invalid:

values = "production-vpc"
7. What Terraform Returns From This Data Source
Once Terraform finds the VPC, it exposes attributes.

Common attributes:

data.aws_vpc.prod_vpc.id
data.aws_vpc.prod_vpc.cidr_block
data.aws_vpc.prod_vpc.arn
data.aws_vpc.prod_vpc.default_security_group_id
Example values:

data.aws_vpc.prod_vpc.id = vpc-123abc
data.aws_vpc.prod_vpc.cidr_block = 10.0.0.0/16
8. How DevOps Engineers Use This in Real Projects
Example: Deploy EC2 into existing VPC.

Existing Infra (Created earlier)

VPC
 ├─ private-subnet
 ├─ public-subnet
 └─ security-group
Terraform fetches VPC:

data "aws_vpc" "prod_vpc" {
  filter {
    name   = "tag:Name"
    values = ["production-vpc"]
  }
}
Then use it:

resource "aws_security_group" "app" {

  vpc_id = data.aws_vpc.prod_vpc.id

  name = "app-sg"

}
Here Terraform uses the existing VPC ID.

9. Real DevOps Project Pattern
In real companies:

Network Team
     │
     ├── VPC
     ├── Subnets
     └── Route Tables
     
DevOps Team
     │
     └── Applications
DevOps must reuse existing network.

So they use data sources.

10. Multiple Filters Example
You can combine filters.

Example:

data "aws_vpc" "prod_vpc" {

  filter {
    name   = "tag:Environment"
    values = ["prod"]
  }

  filter {
    name   = "cidr"
    values = ["10.0.0.0/16"]
  }

}
This means:

Environment = prod
AND
CIDR = 10.0.0.0/16
11. How Terraform Stores the Result Internally
Terraform state stores something like:

data.aws_vpc.prod_vpc

id = vpc-123abc
cidr_block = 10.0.0.0/16
You can reference anywhere:

data.aws_vpc.prod_vpc.id
12. How Terraform Evaluates Data Sources
Order of execution:

terraform init
      │
terraform plan
      │
      ▼
Terraform queries AWS
      │
      ▼
Fetch existing VPC
      │
      ▼
Store values
      │
      ▼
Resources use those values
13. Important Rule
Data source must return exactly one resource.

If Terraform finds:

0 VPCs
Error:

no matching VPC found
If Terraform finds:

2 VPCs
Error:

multiple VPCs matched
So your filter must be unique.

14. Production DevOps Best Practice
Instead of filter, many teams use direct ID.

Example:

data "aws_vpc" "prod_vpc" {
  id = "vpc-123abc"
}
This is safer.

